text:
Prohibition icons indicate actions that must not be performed.  

<PIC:fax_01>
{{image description: Red prohibition symbol: a red circle with diagonal slash and no additional pictogram inside.}}

This icon indicates that flammable sprays must not be used.  

<PIC:fax_02>
{{image description: Red prohibition symbol over a hand inserting or handling a small object, indicating the action is not allowed.}}

This icon indicates that organic solvents such as alcohol, or other liquids must not be used.  

<PIC:fax_03>
{{image description: Red prohibition symbol over a liquid bottle and droplet icon, indicating liquid or chemical use is not allowed.}}

Electrical Hazard icons alert you to possible electrical shock.  

<PIC:fax_04>
{{image description: Black triangular electrical hazard warning icon with a lightning bolt inside.}}

Fire Hazard icons alert you to the possibility of a fire.  

<PIC:fax_05>
{{image description: Black triangular fire hazard warning icon with a flame inside.}}

**CAUTION:**

Wait until pages have exited the product before picking them up. Failure to do this may cause injury to your fingers by trapping them inside the machine.  DO NOT put your hand or any foreign objects into the ink insertion slot. Doing this may cause injury.  If the tray has been extended to hold large paper, position the product so that the tray does not protrude past the edge of the table or desk. If someone hits the tray, the product could fall and cause injury.

<PIC:Manual15_6>
{{image description: Placement illustration of a multifunction fax/printer on a table with paper trays extended; a red prohibition mark appears beside the left example.}}

To prevent injuries, be careful not to put your fingers in the areas shown in the illustrations.  

<PIC:Manual15_7>
{{image description: Four prohibited handling illustrations for a fax/printer: hands under the scanner cover, hands inside or near openings, and hands near the side or rear area, each marked with red prohibition symbols.}}

When changing the tray size from the large paper size to the original size, be careful not to pinch your fingers in the gaps or slots in the bottom of the tray. It may cause injury to you.  

<PIC:Manual15_8>
{{image description: Paper tray illustration showing arrows for sliding or adjusting guides in the tray, plus a second view of hands pushing a tray component inward.}}

(MFC-J6540DW/MFC-J6555DW/MFC-J6740DW/MFC-J6940DW/MFC-J6955DW)  Be careful not to put your fingers in the areas shown in the illustrations. It may cause injury to you.  

  (MFC-J5955DW/MFC-J6540DW/MFC-J6555DW/MFC-J6740DW/MFC-J6940DW/MFC-J6955DW)  
<PIC:Manual15_9>
{{image description: Fax/printer rear or internal area illustration with a red prohibition symbol; an inset shows a hand near a row of internal rollers or mechanisms.}}

To prevent possible injuries, at least two people should lift the product. One person should hold the front of the product, and one person should hold the back, as shown in the illustration below. Carry the product by sliding your hands into the handhold indentations located on each side of the product. Be careful not to trap your fingers when you put the product down.  

<PIC:fax_08>
{{image description: Handling illustration showing one-person and two-person lifting positions around the fax/printer, with red prohibition marks over improper holds.}}

DO NOT carry the product by holding the areas shown in the illustrations. Doing this may cause the product to slip out of your hands and may result in injury.  

<PIC:Manual15_10>
{{image description: Multiple prohibited lifting/handling diagrams for the fax/printer, including insets of side handles, front panel, and lower grips; one label reads MFC-J5955DW.}}

(MFC-J5340DW/MFC-J5855DW)  Carry the product by sliding your hands into the handhold indentations located on each side of the product.  

<PIC:Manual15_11>
{{image description: Correct lifting diagram showing both hands holding the lower side grips of the fax/printer.}}

When carrying the product, remove the trays if they have been expanded to hold large paper. The weight of the paper could cause the trays to fall and cause injury to you or others.  

<PIC:Manual15_12>
{{image description: Prohibited lifting diagram showing hands holding the machine in unsuitable positions near the front or lower edges, marked with a red prohibition symbol.}}

When multiple devices, including this product, are connected to a computer using USB cables, you may feel an electric charge when you touch metal parts of the product.  If the ink contacts your skin or gets into your eye or mouth, follow these steps immediately:  - If your skin comes into contact with the ink, wash your skin with water and soap immediately. - If the ink gets into your eye, rinse it with water, and consult your doctor immediately. If left as is, it may cause redness or mild inflammation of the eye. - If the ink gets into your mouth or you swallow it, spit it out, rinse your mouth, and consult your doctor immediately. Failure to seek medical attention could lead to sickness.  

